{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router", "label": "Router (lokaler Pool-Router)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Ein Actor, dessen einzige Aufgabe es ist, jede eingehende Nachricht an einen oder mehrere Routees weiterzuleiten. Aufrufer sehen eine einzelne ActorRef und wissen nie, wie viele Routees existieren.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_clusterrouter", "label": "ClusterRouter", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Das mitgliedschafts-getriebene Cluster-Aequivalent: Routees werden aus Up-Members plus einem Routee-Pfad abgeleitet, nicht gespawnt. Gleiche externe Schnittstelle wie der lokale Router; der Unterschied ist, was auf der anderen Seite ist.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_wann_router", "label": "Wann zu einem Router greifen", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Vier Muster: CPU-lastige Arbeit parallelisieren ohne das Ordering INNERHALB eines Routees zu brechen; Last ueber role-gefilterte Nodes verteilen; Arbeit per Consistent-Hashing deterministisch an einen Routee pinnen; und N Routees um dieselbe Antwort rennen lassen \u2014 letzteres zielt auf Tail-Latenz, nicht auf Durchsatz.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "label": "Die fuenf Routing-Strategien", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "round-robin (Default), random, broadcast, smallest-mailbox und cluster-only consistent-hashing. Alle fuenf sind One-Shot: der Router waehlt, leitet weiter, fertig \u2014 die Antwort ist Sache des Routees und des urspruenglichen Senders.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router_supervision", "label": "Router und Supervision", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Der Router ist ein regulaerer Actor: er supervised und watcht jeden Routee. Ein neu gestarteter Routee tritt am selben Pfad wieder bei, und was waehrend des Restart-Fensters geroutet wurde, bleibt in seiner Mailbox \u2014 sie wird suspendiert und wieder aufgenommen, nicht gedrained.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_alternativen", "label": "Router sind nicht der einzige Weg zur Parallelisierung", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Sharding ist richtig, wenn jede Arbeitseinheit einen Key hat und genau ein lebender Actor pro Key gebraucht wird; DistributedPubSub ist richtig fuer Fan-Out mit dynamischer Subscriber-Menge. Routing ist ein Pool fester Groesse mit deterministischer Strategie.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_reference_glossary_router", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_reference_glossary_routee", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_clusterrouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_strategies_routingstrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_strategies_round_robin", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_strategies_random", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_strategies_broadcast", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_strategies_smallest_mailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_fuenf_strategien", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_strategies_consistent_hashing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router_supervision", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_reference_glossary_mailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_alternativen", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_reference_glossary_clustersharding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_alternativen", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_reference_glossary_distributedpubsub", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_wann_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_scatter_gather_hedged_request", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_overview_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_routing_pool_vs_group_pool_router", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "